  "reason": "RNA single-profile PCA is currently much stronger than image ResNet (accuracy 0.485 vs 0.208; F1 0.464 vs 0.172), so RNA is the more promising direction. The key uncertainty is whether multiprofile aggregation can improve the RNA representation without changing the encoder. config_002 keeps the same pca_n2000 RNA encoder and adds only multiprofile avgpool, the simplest aggregation option, directly testing the profile/aggregation effect. It is a low-complexity extension of the current best baseline and will clarify whether multiprofile settings are worth pursuing before testing transformer aggregation or multimodal fusion."
}

